{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|pétiole}}, and its source, {{der|en|LL.|petiolus||little foot}}, diminutive form of {{der|en|la|pes}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɛtɪəʊl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpɛdiˌoʊl/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} The [[stalk]] of a [[leaf]], attaching the [[blade]] to the [[stem]].
# {{lb|en|entomology}} A narrow or constricted [[segment]] of the body of an [[insect]]. Used especially to refer to the [[metasomal]] segment of [[Hymenoptera]] such as wasps.
# {{lb|en|entomology}} The stalk at the base of the nest of the [[paper wasp]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|segment of the body of an insect}} {{l|en|pedicel}}

